    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "交脛也。从大，象交形。凡交之屬皆从交。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Pictogram (象形) – a human with crossed legs. In today's writing, the upper part of the human is similar to 立, which in turn depicts a man standing. Unrelated to 父.\nFrom Proto-Sino-Tibetan *rjaw (“mix”); cognate with Burmese ရော (rau:, “to mix”), Jingpho yau (“be mixed”), kəjau (“to mix, intermix”), compare Chepang [script needed] (ljawh-ʔo, “mixed”) and Proto-Mienic *klaau³ (Schuessler, 2007)."
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "For pronunciation and definitions of 交 – see 跤 (“tumble; fall; leg; foot; lower limb; etc.”).\n(This character is the second-round simplified form of 跤).\n Notes:\nSimplified Chinese is mainly used in Mainland China, Malaysia, and Singapore.\nTraditional Chinese is mainly used in Hong Kong, Macau, and Taiwan.\nCompare Teochew 邀 (giao1)."
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "交脛也。从大，象交形。凡交之屬皆从交。",
